        "id": 1344513
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-10T21:05:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "from my understanding in the spec, HF can initiate codec negotiation at anytime by sending a AT+BCC.  So we should go through codec negotiation when it\u0027s received.",
      "parentUuid": "24a0f963_1a20786f",
      "revId": "25579c921a1753ac543a2578201065a75d746888",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b7c934a3_e2246e0c",
        "filename": "system/bta/ag/bta_ag_cmd.cc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1350,
      "author": {
        "id": 1344513
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-25T23:19:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looking at the spec, if the HF wants to initiate codec negotiation, it sends an AT+BAC.  I agree with Bhaktha that we might not want every device to go through codec negotiation when the AG receives an AT+BCC due to efficiency.  Why are we forcing codec negotiating when an AT+BCC is received by the AG?\n\nSatish, in response to your comment, you probably won\u0027t see any issues since the AG can request codec negotiation but the key point is do you want to for efficiency?",
      "parentUuid": "1a73e32b_85cd6cd6",
      "revId": "25579c921a1753ac543a2578201065a75d746888",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0a8cac6b_8f989970",
        "filename": "system/bta/ag/bta_ag_cmd.cc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1350,
      "author": {
        "id": 1902235
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-26T11:41:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "HF sends AT+BAC after SLC only when a codec is available or unavailable.\n\nAgree that doing codec negotiation again when HF wants SCO connection is not efficient. But, we would like to be good to HF which wants codec negotiation and chosen to do codec negotiation again so that SCO goes through and end user can use his/her HF for call functionality.",
      "parentUuid": "b7c934a3_e2246e0c",
      "revId": "25579c921a1753ac543a2578201065a75d746888",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7ecd4f6c_2568bb0c",
        "filename": "system/bta/ag/bta_ag_cmd.cc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1350,
      "author": {
        "id": 1344513
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-26T17:57:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I suggest then that you create an interop fix for this since we don\u0027t want all headsets to go through codec negotiation when the AG receives an AT+BCC since it\u0027s not efficient.  The AT+BAC specifically allows the HF to go through codec negotiation.",
      "parentUuid": "0a8cac6b_8f989970",
      "revId": "25579c921a1753ac543a2578201065a75d746888",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
